{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Before they lay down, and the men of the city, the men of Sodom.</b> Thus it is expounded in Bereshit Rabbah: ״Before they lay down, and the men of the city״ — they were in their mouths, the angels: they were asking Lot what was their nature and their deeds, and he would tell them, most of them are wicked; while they were still speaking of them, ״and the men of Sodom, etc.״ And the plain sense of Scripture: ״And the men of the city״ — men of wickedness; they gathered around the house. Because they were wicked they are called ״men of Sodom,״ as Scripture says: ״Now the men of Sodom were wicked and sinners.״" "<b>All the people from the edge.</b> From one edge of the city to the other — that not one of them raised a hand against them, for there was not even one righteous man among them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:24.263298715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}